dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.constr.op]/2: a conjunction checks its first operand and is not
satisfied if that is not, without substituting into the second.  The
partial specialization pick<T, 1> requires `requires { typename
ref_of_t<T>; } && conv_v<ref_of_t<T>, T>'; for T = int the first operand
is false and the second is ill-formed.  The front end type-checked the
whole conjunction, the second operand failed, and the clause was taken as
satisfied, so pick<int> selected pick<int, 1>.  The shape of libstdc++
16's __common_reference_impl<_Tp1, _Tp2, 1> (common_reference_t<int &,
long &>, cpp20_common_reference_int_lvalue_rvalue with GCC 16).  Fails on
bin53.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.
